WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.820
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and everyone
had a bunch of questions after sign of three

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.290
so I picked twenty from the comments on my
review video to answer.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.950
A lot of you asked very similar questions
so I’ve just combined some of them.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.390
I’m doing my breakdown on wednesday that
will cover all of the references to the books

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.619
and other shows like Doctor Who.

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:25.850
I’ve even seen a hobbit reference.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.960
Also a lot of you asked questions about my
theories about the plot of episode 3 and the

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:30.960
main villain.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.870
I’ll go into that more during the breakdown.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.510
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.400
There are a couple shows that I normally do
that are coming back this week so we’re

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.600
almost back to our normal video schedule.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.360
Since this video goes into specific details
for sherlock series 3 episode 2 careful for

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.130
spoilers if you haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.960
So lot of stuff to get through so let’s
get started.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.370
Number 1 - Ian McGregor asks Please explain
how the murder knife worked.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:05.100
So the Jonathan small, aka the wedding photographer
aka the mayfly man used a very thin knife

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.230
to stab both bainbridge, during the case of
the bloody guardsman and major sholto at the

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.230
wedding.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.640
He did it through their belts, so the knife
had to be super thin and super sharp.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.039
They didn’t feel it because the knife was
so sharp that it just felt like a prick.

00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:23.140
He basically stabbed them and the idea was
that they would slowly bleed to death internally.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.920
Question 2 - Jake Bamford Eldson asks why
do you think it was mycroft that was helping

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.659
sherlock in his mind palace instead of watson?

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:35.049
Sherlock manifested mycroft in his head because
either consciously or subconsciously he thought

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:39.450
that mycroft was the best person to help him
deduce the mayfly man.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.640
Sherlock has already demonstrated that he
thinks mycroft is smarter than he is as seen

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.990
in empty hearse.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.270
So his mind just summoned the smartest person
he knew.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:53.179
Question 3 - Matthew Staton asks, was the
main villian of this series in the book?

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:58.200
If you’re talking about jonathan small lord
stabbington, then yes he’s based on a character

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.829
named small in the book the sign of four which
is what this episode is loosely inspired by.

00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:04.920
The plot is entirely different but I’ll
talk more about that during my breakdown.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.530
If you’re talking about Charles Augustus
Magnussen, then no, he wasn’t part of the

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:12.620
original story, he is mentioned briefly during
sherlock’s wedding speech though.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.310
That will also be in my breakdown video.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.430
Question 4 - Milena Torres asks do you think
the end of episode three will be a cliffhanger

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.760
for season 4?

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.950
Yes, when benedict cumberbatch and martin
freeman signed on for series 3 they also signed

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.040
on for series 4.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.650
I’ll talk mostly about the plot of his last
vow when I do my videos for that episode next

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:30.650
week.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.660
But yes, we are guaranteed a classic sherlock
style cliffhanger.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.069
Question 5 - Lin Robinson asks, what do you
think the connection between Mary and the

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:40.420
main villain, charles augustus magnussen is?

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.140
I’ll talk about this in great detail during
my breakdown, but for now I’ll say that

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.030
when sherlock was reading the notes from people
at the wedding, one of the notes was from

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.030
the villain.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.030
A nickname was used, not his full name.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.760
So you can either re-watch that scene to try
and guess or just wait for my breakdown video

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.860
on wednesday.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.650
But the fact that he sent her a wedding note
that was read aloud should give you an idea

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.670
of how close they are.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:06.480
Question 6 - the sherlockedavatar asks how
do you think sherlock will handle being isolated

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.510
since the sign of three doesn’t include
him?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.159
So you’re asking about what’s going to
happen to sherlock now that watson has a wife

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:13.390
and a baby?

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:16.750
Remember how sherlock carried watson around
in his head for those two years while he was

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.750
away.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.319
When he was solving crimes with molly he kept
talking to mind palace watson.

00:03:21.319 --> 00:03:23.100
The same thing will happen here.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.319
Sherlock will still talk to the two of them
as if they’re always in the room with him.

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:29.220
And his vow was that he would protect them.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.180
So he’ll have to be involved with their
lives.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:37.780
So short answer, he’ll be lonely and use
the mind palace a lot, but watson and mary

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.780
aren’t going to desert him.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.659
I think they consider him part of their family
even if sherlock doesn’t see it that way.

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:48.080
Question 7 - Fangirl1502 asks how will sherlock’s
last vow tie into the last episode?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.900
The vow implied that he would die for the
three of them if need be and he’d stop at

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.510
nothing to protect them.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.210
So I think he’ll end up in a situation that
he can’t solve.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.640
He’ll have to make a choice that will mean
the death of one character over another.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:07.030
Whether it’s his own death or mycrofts or
watsons or marys.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:13.049
Martin Freeman signed a contract for series
4, so I think we can assume he won’t die

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:14.459
or benedict cumberbatch.

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:19.420
Question 8 - Mahmoud Lakhnavi asks what are
the true intentions of mary, is she good or

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:21.859
bad and what about news for series 4?

00:04:21.859 --> 00:04:26.540
So mary is a good character, but remember
when sherlock deduced her it said disillusioned.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.500
She has the wrong idea about a certain person
that will be critical to the plot of episode

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.500
3.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.500
So no she’s not evil.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.240
As for series 4, right now all we know is
that the actors have signed contracts.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.100
I’ll be doing a predictions video after
episode 3 airs though.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.920
Question 9 - FruityGaim asks is it the murder
game?

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.440
So you’re asking about the question I asked
you guys in my review video.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.750
I said try to guess the new party game I was
going to try.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:57.100
It was actually drunk deductions.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.260
Eggy chair sitty thing.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:03.670
Question 10 - Solaris290 asks were you surprised
to see donovan?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.890
Yes, she wasn’t available for filming when
they were making episode 1, but the interesting

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:12.140
thing is that all of those scenes at the beginning
of the episode happened around the time sherlock

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.140
came back.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.570
There was about 6 months between the events
of the last episode which took place in november

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.780
and this episode which is in may.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.980
So donovan was around in november, but you
don’t see her at all during the current

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.130
time on the show.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:27.090
So either she just wasn’t invited or something
happened to her in that 6 months.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.470
Anderson isn’t around either.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.330
Maybe the two of them started doin it again.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.540
Question 11 - Flora3722 asks why is mycroft
wearing a wedding ring?

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:41.720
You have a good eye, when we see mycroft talking
to sherlock we see a ring on his right hand.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.510
Most western cultures wear the wedding ring
on the left hand.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:53.290
But it can also be worn on the right hand
as a sign of commitment or if it’s a family

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.290
heirloom.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.880
Mark Gatiss has addressed the ring on his
twitter saying definitively that mycroft was

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:56.880
not married.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.550
He said that it was a prop and it was intentional
on the part of the production team.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:04.280
But he wouldn’t explain what it meant.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:08.560
Anthea has a ring on her right hand too, so
let the theories fly.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:09.560
I’ll talk more about it during my breakdown
video.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:14.230
Question 12 - Kristine Silmaro asks why was
the episode called sign of three?

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:18.670
The plot was inspired by elements of the sign
of four book and A lot of the characters names

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.060
like Small and major sholto.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:26.530
Sign of four involved this treasure plot that
mary morstan got tied up in, so a lot of things

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.530
were changed.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:32.130
Question 13 - Marysol Losada asks is mary
standing in front of the horns foreshadowing?

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.630
it makes it look like they’re coming out
of her head.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:38.640
This is both a funny reference to her being
a bit of a trickster.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.120
She was playing both sherlock and watson to
get them out of the house so she could plan

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.120
the wedding.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.570
But I actually do think it’s a general ominous
warning that there is a supernatural aspect

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:51.700
to her character, supernatural in the sense
that her character is much larger than what

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.310
the story has presented her as so far.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.310
Good eye.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.860
Plus that thumbs up moment was one of the
best jifs from the episode.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:03.490
Question 14 - Wensley Talleyrand asks will
we see more of sherlock and the bridesmaid?

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.720
Only in hetero fan fiction.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:10.770
Their final scene where she said I wish you
weren’t the way you are and he said me too.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:14.120
Just means they’re both acknowledging that
they’re never going to be a thing.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.590
Sherlock is too sherlock for his own good.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:22.320
I’m sure if you search tumblr you can find
a little sherlock bridsemaid fic though.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.150
Question 15 - siis saia asks what did red
beard mean when mycroft talked to sherlock

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:28.260
on the phone?

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.250
Mycroft was talking about the end of an era.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:34.870
Redbeard and his brother were pirates together
and after his brother died redbeard continued

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.510
the tradition.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:40.000
So mycroft was just telling sherlock that
he’d always be there for him and that after

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.870
the loss of watson (who is basically sherlock’s
other brother) sherlock would have to carry

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:48.950
on his work alone.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:52.970
Question 16 - Devyn Straushbaugh asks do you
think we’ll see that one character from

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.570
the mind palace again this season?

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:58.380
No, not this series, but possibly another
cameo next series.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.039
They don’t retread a lot of stories, so
I don’t expect her to get her own episode

00:08:00.039 --> 00:08:01.039
again.

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:03.720
She’ll never be completely gone as long
as she’s rattling around naked in sherlock’s

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:04.720
head.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:08.350
Question 17 - wh0urgrl asks will you do more
sherlock videos when it airs in the united

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.190
states?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:15.920
Yes, they’ll be a little bit different,
but yes I’ll do something fun.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.240
I might even do a giveaway.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:18.360
Awesome channel by the way.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.360
Keep making videos!

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.560
Question 18 - MariaVosa asks, what was up
with mary’s shirt?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.490
You’re talking about the thumbs up shirt.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:24.800
That was funny and weird.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:25.800
I definitely got a vibe from her.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.540
I think it was just meant to be funny and
just reinforce the idea that she thinks of

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.650
herself as a trickster.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:37.539
She would have chosen to wear that shirt knowing
full well that she was giving them a thumbs

00:08:37.539 --> 00:08:39.310
up while wearing it.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.610
There are no coincidences on sherlock.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.090
Everything has a purpose.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:47.890
Question 19 - Yuki ame asks how do you think
mycroft would react if he thought sherlock

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:48.890
died?

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:52.860
And is sherlock becoming more social going
to hurt his abilities to solve crimes?

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.829
Good questions, I think mycroft would feel
an approximation of sadness.

00:08:56.829 --> 00:09:00.199
Mark Gatiss’ version of the character is
much warmer than the book version.

00:09:00.199 --> 00:09:02.620
He wouldn’t cry, but he would bring sherlock’s
killer to swift justice

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:06.250
And yes, I do think sherlock’s ability to
solve crimes will be affected now that he’s

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:09.389
so emotionally involved with watson, mary
and the baby.

00:09:09.389 --> 00:09:13.610
I think that will play more into episode 3.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:20.490
and question 20, last one - Ether says sherlock
is starting to explore the characters emotions

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:24.199
too much and less on the pure strain of his
core self.

00:09:24.199 --> 00:09:25.519
The puzzle solver.

00:09:25.519 --> 00:09:28.079
You actually had a pretty epic comment, high
fives.

00:09:28.079 --> 00:09:32.220
This was a pretty common complaint I saw from
a lot of you guys.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:36.819
I’ll say that yes, this series more so than
in previous series the character has swung

00:09:36.819 --> 00:09:41.370
back and forth to both ends of the emotional
spectrum and has been profoundly weird.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:45.860
In empty hearse he was completely disconnected
from watson in a human sense and now the three

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.670
or four of them depending on how you look
are turning into a family unit.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:54.709
There was an anime episode i just did a video
for and the title was once more, with feeling.

00:09:54.709 --> 00:09:55.740
Which reminded me of joss whedon’s buffy,
so I think the alternate title of this episode

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.529
is sherlock, once more with feeling.

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:03.600
What I think we’ll see in episode 3 is that
pendulum swing back to the middle.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:11.690
He’s gone from super detached to super attached
and by the end of series 3 he’ll be back

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:14.950
to that middle ground puzzle solver you were
talking about.

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:18.380
So thank you so much everyone for submitting
your questions, I hope my answers covered

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.380
most of everything.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:22.210
Like i said i’ll be doing a full breakdown
of the episode that will deal with a lot more

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:24.749
of the specific details and provide some contextual
clues for what’s going to happen during

00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:25.749
episode 3.

00:10:25.749 --> 00:10:26.749
Be sure to subscribe to get that video.

00:10:26.749 --> 00:10:27.749
I’ll try to post it by wednesday.

00:10:27.749 --> 00:10:31.319
Remember nothing on the show is a coincidence,
everything has a purpose, the clothes they

00:10:31.319 --> 00:10:33.980
wear, the way their scenes are filmed and
the things they say.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.829
Right now click here for my review of the
episode and click here for my breakdown of

00:10:37.829 --> 00:10:38.829
episode 1.

00:10:38.829 --> 00:10:40.839
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow!

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:41.439
high fives!

